{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>And as for all the mighty hand.</b> That the El wrought through him upon perishable things, changing their nature — such as the splitting of the sea, the opening of the mouth of the earth, the bringing down of the manna from the heavens, and similar things." "<b>And as for all the great terror.</b> That of the giving of the Torah." "<b>Which Moses wrought before the eyes of all Israel.</b> When they saw and stood afar off at the giving of the Torah, while Moses drew near to the thick darkness — for then he attained the supreme degree of prophecy, face to face. And Moses was then made awesome with beams of splendor." "<b>Before the eyes of all Israel.</b> As it says: וַיַּרְא אַהֲרֹן וְכָל בְּנֵי יִשְׂרָאֵל אֶת מֹשֶׁה כִּי קָרַן עוֹר פָּנָיו וַיִּירְאוּ מִגֶּשֶׁת אֵלָיו (Exodus 34:30). Thus concludes the portion of VeZot HaBerakhah."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 34, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:23:49.174207483Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}